  - Omitted unrelated grilled pompano / tomato-lemon salsa recipe from the source document
---

> Assemble each quesadilla in the skillet while the tortilla cooks — neat and easy. Do not overload the filling; you want them pleasantly crisp, not soggy.

Put a rack in the middle of the #oven{}, set a large heatproof #plate{} on the rack, and preheat to 200°F.

In a #bowl{}, stir together @pepper Jack cheese{1 1/2%cups}(coarsely grated, about 5 oz), @black beans{1/2%cup}(from 1 can, drained and rinsed), @fresh cilantro{2%tbsp}(finely chopped), and @ground cumin{1/2%tsp}.

Heat about 1/2 teaspoon of the @vegetable oil{1-2%tbsp} in an #8-inch nonstick skillet{} over moderate heat until hot but not smoking. Add 1 of the @flour tortillas{8}(6-inch) and top the half nearest you with 2 to 3 tablespoons of the cheese mixture, spreading it evenly. Spread about 1 tablespoon of the @chunky salsa{1/2%cup} over the cheese mixture. Using a spatula, fold the uncovered half of the tortilla over and cook until the underside is golden, about ~{1%minute}. Carefully turn the quesadilla and cook until the underside is golden, about ~{1-2%minutes} more. Transfer to the plate in the oven and cover loosely with foil.

Make 7 more quesadillas the same way, adding about 1/2 teaspoon oil to the skillet for each and dividing the remaining cheese mixture and salsa among them. Stack finished quesadillas on the plate in the oven. Serve warm.
